-- title:
--   §2, pp. 5–6 — regular discrete choice model, revenue, OPT and revenue-ordered (threshold) assortments
-- statement:
--   This module fixes the general assortment model of §2 of Berbeglia and Joret.
--
--   Let $\mathcal C$ be a finite set of products. A **system of choice probabilities** assigns to every offered set $S\subseteq\mathcal C$ and every product $x\in\mathcal C$ the probability $\mathcal P(x,S)$ that a consumer offered $S$ buys $x$; the probability of buying nothing is
--   $$
--   \mathcal P(0,S)=1-\sum_{x\in S}\mathcal P(x,S).
--   $$
--   The system is **regular** if it satisfies the paper's four axioms:
--
--   1. (i) $\mathcal P(x,S)\ge 0$ for every product $x$, and $\mathcal P(0,S)\ge 0$;
--   2. (ii) $\mathcal P(x,S)=0$ whenever $x\notin S$;
--   3. (iii) $\sum_{x\in S}\mathcal P(x,S)\le 1$;
--   4. (iv) $\mathcal P(x,S)\ge\mathcal P(x,S')$ whenever $S\subseteq S'$ and $x\in S\cup\{0\}$ — both for products $x\in S$ and for the no-purchase option $0$.
--
--   Given revenues $r:\mathcal C\to\mathbb R$, the revenue of an offered set is $\mathrm{rev}(S)=\sum_{x\in S}\mathcal P(x,S)\,r(x)$, and $\mathrm{OPT}=\max_{S\subseteq\mathcal C}\mathrm{rev}(S)$ (the empty set is allowed and earns $0$). For a product $y$, the **revenue-ordered assortment** generated by $y$ is $\{y'\in\mathcal C: r(y')\ge r(y)\}$.
--
--   These are the objects in which Theorem 4.16 phrases the assortment side of the correspondence.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Products form a finite type `C`; the no-purchase option is not a product and $\mathcal P(0,S)$ is the derived quantity `noPurchase`. The $x=0$ case of axiom (i) is included explicitly (it also follows from (iii)); the $x=0$ case of axiom (iv) is the field `noPurchase_mono`. OPT is a `Finset.sup'` over all subsets of `C`.
-- source:
--   Berbeglia & Joret, Assortment Optimisation Under a General Discrete Choice Model: A Tight Analysis of Revenue-Ordered Assortments, arXiv:1606.01371v3, pp. 5–7, §2 (axioms (i)–(iv)), Definition 1, §3

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RevenueOrdered_Ratio_Model

namespace RevenueOrdered.Stackelberg

open Classical in
/-- The RevenueOrdered.Ratio.revenue-ordered assortment generated by the product `y`: all products `y'` with
`r(y') ≥ r(y)` (§3, p. 7, and the statement of Theorem 4.16, p. 24). -/
noncomputable def thresholdSet {C : Type*} [Fintype C] (r : C → ℝ) (y : C) : Finset C :=
  Finset.univ.filter (fun y' => r y ≤ r y')

end RevenueOrdered.Stackelberg


